            <div xml:id="d42">

                <pb facs="0107" n="73" xml:id="pg73"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">THE UNITED STATES LEGATION IN PARIS TO THE
                    DEPARTMENT OF STATE.</note>
                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 42.</note>
                <head>Mr. W. Hoffman to Mr.
                        Fish.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Received 9.30 a. m. July 16,
                        1870.]</seg></opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1870-07-15"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 15, 1870.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fish,</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Washington:</hi></p>
                <p>War is certain. Can I take Prussian subjects in France under our protection? Have
                    promised answer to-morrow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HOFFMAN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
